# Story 27: Pane & Tab Navigation (45s)
# Hook: Move through your workspace without lifting your hands from the keyboard.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-027-pane-tab-navigation.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Move through your workspace without lifting your hands from the keyboard.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. We'll build out a few panes and tabs so there is something to navigate.

[00:08.0 --> 00:15.0]
Ctrl+P then n splits a pane to the right. Ctrl+T then n opens a fresh tab.

[00:15.0 --> 00:24.0]
Press Tab to cycle to the next pane. Alt+Up and Alt+Down step between panes too.

[00:24.0 --> 00:34.0]
Brackets move between tabs -- left bracket back, right bracket forward. Alt+Left and Alt+Right do the same.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
On macOS, Option plus arrow can be tricky, so Alt+B and Alt+F also walk between your tabs.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
One muscle memory for panes, one for tabs. That is your whole workspace.

